WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.201
-My first guest is an Oscar-

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.970
and Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.105
who stars in the new movie
"Joe Bell,"

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.641
which is in theaters July 23rd.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.077
Please welcome Mark Wahlberg.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.078
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.213
Hey, hey, hey!

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.715
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:18.118
Welcome, buddy.
-Hey.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.353
It's so crazy
doing this like this.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.721
-It's -- It's wild.
It's bizarre.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.822
But we have a full audience now,
so we're baby steps.

00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:25.158
We're coming back, buddy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.059
-I can't -- I cannot --

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:29.195
Cannot wait to come back
and visit in person.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.631
-Yeah, me, too.
I know you're back in L.A.,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.798
safe with the kids.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.000
How is the family doing?
Everyone good?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.236
-Uh, yeah.
Everybody's hanging in there.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.539
It's been tough
with COVID and Zooms.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.908
And now that school's over,
I don't see kids usually

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.176
till about 2:00 or 3:00
in the afternoon.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.178
They start waking up,
and then they don't really

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.279
come out until they're done
playing their video games.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:51.217
They're looking for food
or looking for Taki chips.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.253
-Takis.
-Yeah, they love the Takis.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.521
-Oh, yeah,
who doesn't love the Takis?

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.123
It is a big thing.
-I mention that now.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.359
Boxes are gonna show up.
-I know! Exactly right.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.895
-It's a bad idea.
-You must have had some Takis

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.931
on this last movie
that you just wrapped,

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:07.133
which, hopefully, you'll
come back, we'll talk about.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.235
I think it's called "Stu,"
right now.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.603
-Yeah.
-It's about --

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.939
Is it about a boxer
turned priest, or...?

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.040
Well, we'll get into it.
-Yeah, it's a true story.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.542
He was a boxer.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:19.045
He tried to become an actor.
He fell in love.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.548
And in order to kind of
win the girl over,

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.383
he wanted to get baptized,

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:25.751
and then he had
this horrific accident.

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:27.720
And then he wanted to go --
Once he got baptized,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.622
he wanted to go all the way,
and he became a priest.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.823
It's a true story.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.893
-This is a picture of you
filming the movie, right?

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.461
-Yep.
That's as a boxer.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.263
-Yeah,
and then three weeks later,

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.931
and this is not --
I'm not making this up.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:43.369
Three weeks later,
this is a picture of Mark.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.338
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.807
-Dude, how?
I mean, how is that possible?

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.241
-It's the mustache.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.477
[ Laughter ]
It's the mustache.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.146
-That's what did it?
It looks --

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:57.049
-Unfortunately, I had to consume
for two weeks 7,000 calories,

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.019
and then for another two weeks,
11,000 calories.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.555
And it was fun
for about an hour.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.357
And then --
You know, it's just such a --

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:07.459
It's such a physical --
a hard, physical thing to do.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.462
I mean, losing weight,
you just kind of tough it out,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.798
you just don't eat
and exercise.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.099
And this, even when you're full,

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.668
I would wake up after a meal
and have another meal.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.769
I was eating every three hours.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.238
It was, uh, not fun.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:20.472
-Is it harder to do?

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:22.174
'Cause -- By the way,
happy belated birthday.

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:23.709
You just turned 50.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:24.944
-Yeah.
Thank you, man.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.146
-He looks like he's 25.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:31.017
Is it harder to do the older you
get, to gain and lose weight?

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:34.120
-Yeah, absolutely.
You know, once the metabolism

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.988
starts to slows down,
it gets really difficult.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:37.623
But, you know,
it was something that --

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.359
I'd been trying to get this
movie made for six years.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.026
We only had 30 days to shoot it.

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:44.364
And so, I wanted
to really make it happen.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.899
And we're also crazy enough

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.435
to have financed
a lot of it myself.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.271
So, I knew I was on a ticking
clock, on my own dime.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.773
And, you know, you get things
done pretty quickly

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.908
when that's the case.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.477
Let's talk about your movie,
"Joe Bell."

00:02:58.477 --> 00:02:59.812
This is cool that you did this.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.781
This is another true story --
based on a true story.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.083
-Yep.
-Can you set up the film

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.252
for everyone?
-Yeah, well, it's --

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.853
I don't want
to give away everything,

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:10.189
but a dad is basically
going on a journey

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.292
from La Grande, Oregon,
to New York City,

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.327
where his son always
wanted to live.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:18.263
And he's talking to anybody
and everybody that he can meet,

00:03:18.263 --> 00:03:22.735
people that he confronts about
intolerance and bullying.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.504
And -- Yeah, he's trying to
raise awareness for his son.

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:28.374
-It's an amazing story.
It's almost hard to believe.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.676
But how did you
find out about this?

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:32.778
-Actually,
somebody sent me the script.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:36.415
And I read it, and I obviously
was very moved by it.

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:38.584
And then, I had realized
that I had seen somewhere,

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:41.654
I think,
on the news about Joe's journey.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.957
But I didn't really --
It didn't really register.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:47.393
And then, of course,
I went up to La Grande

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:52.431
to visit with Lola
and Joseph, with their family.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.967
And I was immediately committed
to making the movie.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:58.570
I just felt like, you know, as
a parent, of course, you know,

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.273
it's such an important story
to be told.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:05.812
-You know -- I think you rethink
everything once you have kids,

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:08.714
especially when it comes
to bullying and stuff.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:09.882
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.751
-Did you read this as an actor
or as a dad?

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.288
-I read it as a dad.
I read it as a dad.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:18.324
And then I cast it as a dad.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:22.595
You know, we put the whole movie
together based on that feeling.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:26.366
And we actually cast an amazing
young actor, Reid Miller.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.334
-Oh, he's great.
-Who, when he came into

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.669
the room -- we auditioned
here at my house --

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:33.739
I mean, he had a lot of
similar mannerisms to my --

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.475
to both of my boys.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.177
And so, I just immediately
felt like it was him.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.579
And, of course,
going through the process,

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:42.214
there was a lot of other
wonderful actors coming through.

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:45.018
But I always, you know,
just gravitated towards Reid.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.118
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.020
Here's Mark Wahlberg
in "Joe Bell."

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.288
Take a look at this.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:50.923
-♪ You're beautiful
in your way ♪

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.525
♪ 'Cause God makes no mistakes ♪
♪ I'm on the right track -- ♪

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:56.162
-♪ ...track, baby,
I was born this way ♪

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.200
-What?
-Well, don't look so surprised.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.068
-Excuse me. I didn't know
you knew the words.

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:05.538
-Well, you blast that so loud,
you think I didn't pick up

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.139
a thing or two downstairs?
-Wow, okay.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.574
-I'm on one of them --
What do you call them?

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.575
♪ I'm a monster ♪
♪ I'm a monster ♪

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.111
-Okay.
-All right --

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.178
-Yeah.
-Excuse me.

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.713
It's "A little monster,"
to be correct.

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:16.081
-A little monster?
-Yeah.

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:17.516
-You know what?
All right, even I'll admit it.

00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:19.151
Okay? It's a little catchy.
-Yes, it is.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.485
-"Don't hide yourself
in regret.

00:05:20.485 --> 00:05:21.754
Just love yourself
and you're set."

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.389
♪ I'm on the right track, baby ♪

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.124
♪ I was born this way ♪
-All right.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.892
-We're not doing that again.

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.361
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.896
-Hey, hey!
You're a good man, buddy.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:32.898
Always good to see you.
Mark Wahlberg.

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:36.903
"Joe Bell"
is in theaters July 23rd.

